aegis-shell (1.7.0-m13) resolute; urgency=medium

  * ONE TRAFFIC-LIGHT ANATOMY, top to bottom — the review round that
    closes the "terminal lines are back / wifi / no battery / DND / no
    boot logo" report. The AegisLights aurorae theme was re-derived from
    the Plasma 6.6 aurorae v2 engine source (plasma/aurorae, the
    decoration moved out of kwin at 6.4): buttons start exactly at
    TitleEdgeLeft with no padding, the caption rect spans between the
    button clusters plus TitleBorderLeft/Right, and borders().top is
    max(TitleHeight, ButtonHeight + ButtonMarginTop) + TitleEdgeTop +
    TitleEdgeBottom. With TitleEdgeLeft 24->18 the measured close dot
    lands at 14 px = the shell's TrafficLights x:14 (the v0.6.20 engine
    predicted 24 and measured 20 — the 4 px gap that motivated the
    re-derivation). ButtonMarginTop 16->6 (plus a ButtonMarginTopMaximized
    6) puts the dot center on the caption text center (top + 22), and
    TitleBorderRight 24->78 re-centres the caption on the true window
    center after the left button cluster (the v0.6.20 caption measured
    30 px right of centre). Dead keys ButtonMarginLeft/Right/Bottom are
    dropped with a comment naming the 6.6 reader set.
  * The title band now paints the shell's glass recipe (T5): the old
    #343740 -> #22242B gradient read 44-55 lum against the Files glass
    band's flat 19 — the "bright band" the user saw. gen-aurorae-frame.py
    (new) paints both frame SVGs flat rgba(16,16,18,0.52) with the shell
    hairlines (white 0.14 active, ~0.06 inactive), so 02-files and
    03-terminal band pixels agree over the same wallpaper.
  * Hover glyphs (T6): Qt.lighter(hue, 3.4) clamps HSV value at 1.0 for
    the close and minimize hues — the shell's hover glyph was rendering
    at the circle's own color, i.e. invisible. TrafficLights.qml and the
    regenerated button SVGs now share explicit hue-tinted whites
    (#FFE7E6 / #FFF5E0 / #E0FFE5).
  * Titles (T4): kdeglobals [WM] activeFont = Montserrat 10 pt DemiBold,
    the same family and weight the first-party app windows use; the
    session already exports QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=kde so KDecoration3
    settings->font() picks it up.
  * Control Center (T8): the TIER chip and its governor popover are gone
    (debug chrome — performance belongs to the Calm Mode tile), the
    footer no longer echoes the live accent hex, and the window keeps
    its Table 17 rhythm.
  * Top bar (T9): the Wi-Fi fan re-centres on the speaker/clock midline
    (cy h/2 + 3.5 -> + 2); the battery glyph itself shipped in a7998f4
    (v0.6.21) and now reaches an ISO tag with this one.
  * The capture harness gains teeth (T7): header_geometry_assert() pins
    the Files CSD band and the aurorae band to one anatomy — dot drop
    top+22 ±4 with parity, dot inset 14 ±5 with parity (the old
    TitleEdgeLeft 24 measures 20 and fails), dot width 12 ±3, and the
    terminal band luminance <= 32. Verified against the v0.6.20 captures:
    the files side passes, the old terminal fails on all four classes.
  * B2: the idle-session plymouth show-splash experiment is renamed
    07-live-splash-probe.png with an explicit not-boot-evidence log line
    — the old "07-plymouth-test" name read as boot proof while the frame
    showed whatever the idle renderer managed, i.e. the "terminal lines
    are back" confusion. Boot evidence stays the boot-NN frames judged
    by splash_report().
  * B3: the SDDM greeter carries the Aegis mark (the transparent plymouth
    watermark, synced as mark.png) with the splash's track + accent
    progress device above the clock — the logo survives past the boot
    splash, and the greeter is now covered by qml-guard.

