aegis-shell (1.7.0-m12) resolute; urgency=medium

  * THE SPLASH BUG, FOUND AND FIXED: the v0.6.24 serial trace shows the
    renderer chain was never broken — plymouthd found card0 (virtio_gpu),
    opened the drm renderer, found the 1280x800 head at 0.96 s, loaded
    the aegis-mark two-step plugin — and then aborted at "loading lock
    image: No such file or directory". plymouth's two-step theme REQUIRES
    lock.png in ImageDir and a failed load kills the whole splash; the
    fallback chain (text theme fails too) lands in the details plugin,
    whose whole job is echoing boot output to the screen. Every black
    frame and every terminal line since v0.6.10 was plymouth's own
    details canvas. The theme now ships lock.png (paper padlock), entry
    .png, bullet.png and box.png — the LUKS prompt assets — generated in
    gen-plymouth-mark.py on the Tokens palette.

