aegis-shell (1.7.0-m10) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Boot-phase plymouthd decisions become visible: plymouth.debug=file:
    on the kernel command line (harness and ISO grub) sends the
    renderer/device scan into /run/plymouth-boot-debug.log, which
    survives switch-root; the capture reads it right after serial login
    so even a failing run ships the why. The v0.6.22 post-mortem: the
    initrd already carried virtio-gpu.ko — the aegis initramfs hook's
    modinfo guard had resolved against the RUNNING kernel (uname) and
    silently skipped every force_load; the guard now resolves per
    installed kernel version, and virtio_gpu/bochs land in conf/modules
    so they load before udev even runs.

 -- Aegis Developers <dev@aegis-os.org>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:05:00 +0000

aegis-shell (1.7.0-m9) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The splash painted nothing because plymouthd never had a renderer:
    the DRM renderer is picked once, at daemon startup, and the initramfs
    shipped no GPU driver (MODULES=most excludes GPU drivers and the
    FRAMEBUFFER hook detects no hardware in a bare build chroot), so
    /dev/dri/card0 did not exist when plymouthd started — v0.6.21 kept
    the daemon alive from ~6 s to plymouth-quit at 26.8 s with zero
    pixels on screen. A new initramfs hook force-loads virtio_gpu (and
    bochs_drm when present) so the card exists BEFORE plymouthd starts at
    init-premount.
  * The boot test failed on its own gates, which is what they are for:
    the DND assert bar sat at 1.0 while a real toggle measures ~0.35 —
    the retry then clicked the switch back off and shipped the identical
    frame again. Bar recalibrated to 0.15 with the panel clock excluded
    from the diff, the retry now uses the tile body, and the splash gate
    fires after the gpu/plymouth diagnostics probe so a failure log
    always carries /dev/dri, lsmod and journal evidence.

